\b Shin Desktop Preview\b0\par
\cf2 A development preview for Windows x64.\cf1\par\par
\b What gets installed\b0\par
Core, Observer, command-line and MCP clients, and Shin Monitor. No WSL, Python, Node or model server is required.\par\par
\b How it runs\b0\par
Installation requires administrator approval. A Windows service supervises separate, unelevated user runtimes. Monitor starts at sign-in; closing its window does not stop Observer.\par\par
\b Your projects stay yours\b0\par
Setup does not enroll projects or rewrite client configuration. Project files, private indexes, history and credentials are outside the package and are preserved during removal.\par\par
\b Maintenance\b0\par
Close Monitor and command-line clients before repair, upgrade or removal. Setup stops this kit's host and user processes before replacing files.\par\par
\b Preview status\b0\par
This is a development candidate, not a Windows Stable release. Graphical project onboarding is not yet enabled.\par\par
\b License and notices\b0\par
Shin is licensed under Apache-2.0. The license and applicable third-party notices are included in the kit under share/shin-observer/licenses and share/shin-context/licenses. These preview notes do not change those licenses.\par
